@startuml 08-user-lifecycle
!include _style.iuml
title Account lifecycle

[*] --> Registering : register-init\n(OTP emailed, nothing in DB yet)
Registering --> Active : verify-otp\n(user row created, welcome email)
Registering --> [*] : OTP expired or\n5 wrong codes

state Active {
  [*] --> Guest
  Guest --> HostPending : submit host request
  HostPending --> Guest : rejected or cancelled
  HostPending --> Host : admin approves\n(+HOTEL_MANAGER role,\nHotelManagerProfile row)
}

Active --> Blocked : admin blocks\n(listings SUSPENDED,\nreviews hidden)
Blocked --> Active : admin unblocks\n(listings and reviews restored)
Active --> Deleted : user deletes account\n(no active bookings,\nnot the last admin)
Deleted --> Active : admin restores\n(within 30 days: everything back)
Deleted --> Purged : nightly job after 30 days\n(photo, reviews, host listings removed)
Purged --> Active : admin restores\n(row kept; data already gone)

note right of Blocked
  isActive = false, blockReason, blockedAt.
  The next request gets 401 ACCOUNT_BLOCKED.
end note
note right of Deleted
  Soft delete: isActive = false, deletedAt set.
  The email stays taken (cannot re-register).
  A restore of a previously blocked user keeps
  the block.
end note
note right of Purged
  purgedAt set once. The users row is kept
  forever: bookings, payments and earnings
  point at its id.
end note
@enduml
